-- title:
--   Rational lookup tables for the finite Mertens endpoint certificate below 512
-- statement:
--   The file bundles the explicit rational lookup tables supporting a finite endpoint certificate for the reciprocal-prime (Mertens-type) estimate for $2\le n\le 511$.
--
--   1. `pl521` is the finite set of the 98 primes $p\le 521$.
--   2. `llb`, `lub` assign to every prime $p\le 521$ rational numbers with $\mathrm{llb}(p)\le\log\log p\le\mathrm{lub}(p)$.
--   3. `T` tabulates the partial reciprocal-prime sums $T(n)=\sum_{p\le n}1/p$ for $0\le n\le 511$ (and $T(n)=0$ for $n>511$) as exact rationals.
--   4. `lastP(n)` (resp. `firstP(n)`) is the largest prime $\le n$ (resp. the smallest prime $\ge n$).
--   5. `wloN`, `wlo`, `WLOi`, `WLO` tabulate $\mathrm{wlo}(p)=\log(1-1/p)+1/p$ at rational scale and its partial sums $WLO(n)=\sum_{p\le n}\mathrm{wlo}(p)$ for $n\le 512$ at scale $10^{-9}$.
--   6. `Mq`, `glo`, `tlo`, `M` are the numerical constants entering the endpoint estimate: $M_q=\frac{32380009}{125000000}$, $\mathrm{glo}=\frac{300367}{40000}-10\cdot\frac{6931471808}{10^{10}}-\frac1{1024}$, $\mathrm{tlo}=WLO(512)-\frac12\bigl(\frac1{512}-\frac1{8192}\bigr)-\frac1{8192}$ and $M=M_q$.
--   7. `rho1f`, `rho1`, `rho2f`, `rho2`, `rho` are the rational endpoint error terms: $\rho_1(n)=\rho_{1f}(\mathrm{lastP}(n),\,n-\mathrm{lastP}(n))$, $\rho_2(n)=\rho_{2f}(\mathrm{firstP}(n),\,\mathrm{firstP}(n)-n-1)$ and $\rho=\rho_1+\rho_2$.
--
--   The tables form the numerical interface consumed by `TaoFivePrimes.mertens_reciprocal_endpoint_certificate_511`: all values are stored as exact rationals (or integers) so that every subsequent inequality is a finite arithmetic check, and no floating-point or analytic input is imported.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** `Nat.primesLE`, `Finset` and the `Rat`/`Real` coercions are used as in the surrounding development. The integer table `clbZ` of `Definitions.Def_TaoFivePrimes_theta_cert_tables` enters only through `rho1f`.
-- source:
--   Auxiliary finite-certificate tables introduced for TaoFivePrimes.mertens_reciprocal_endpoint_certificate_511 (the finite endpoint certificate for the reciprocal-prime estimate, an auxiliary obligation for TaoFivePrimes.mawia_reciprocal_sum_upper_bound_small).

